          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ముత్తాత (muttāta) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4954 lists Telugu muttāta, \"great-grandfather\", and mutt-avva, \"great-grandmother\", in the article of Tamil mutu, \"old\": the old grandfather."
